SPCWD Job Order System
San Pablo City Water District — Desktop Management App
Built with Flutter + Supabase


What This App Does

This is the desktop-side management app for the San Pablo City Water District's job order operations.
Office staff use this to receive water-related complaints from the public, create job orders, assign field teams, track progress, and generate monthly reports — all in one place.

The field teams have a separate mobile app that receives the job assignments and marks them as accomplished.
This desktop app is what the admin and office staff use to manage everything from the backend.


Tech Stack

Framework - Flutter (Desktop)
Backend / Database - Supabase (PostgreSQL)
 Authentication - Custom username + password via `users` table
 Charts - `fl_chart`
PDF Export - `pdf` + `printing` packages
Image Upload - `image_picker` + Supabase Storage

-User Roles

The app has 3 types of users, all stored in the `users` table in Supabase:

`admin` - Full access to everything — all screens, all admin features
 `sub_admin` - Regular user with specific permissions granted by the admin (can access admin panel, edit reports, or both)
 `user` - Standard office staff — can create complaints, assign teams, mark accomplished, view reports

Field teams use a completely separate system the PAMD mobile app via the `profiles` table (not `users`). They log in with a username + password, no email required.


Supabase Database Tables

Here are the main tables the app reads from and writes to:


`users` - Office/admin accounts with roles and permissions
 `profiles` - Field team mobile app accounts (username + password_hash)
 `teams`  Team groups with a foreman, driver, and list of members
 `personnel`  Individual field workers (Team Leaders, Drivers, Members)
 `job_orders` All job orders — pending, accomplished, and deleted
 `skeletal_job`  Unofficial/custom job assignments not tied to formal J.O. numbers
 `work_types`  The dropdown options for "Type of Work" in the job order form
 `damage_spaces`  The dropdown options for "Damaged Working Space" in the form
 `team_notifications`  Notifications sent to the mobile app when jobs are assigned or accomplished
| `team_monthly_logs` Monthly snapshots of each team's lineup (leader, driver, members)
