`skeletal_team_screen.dart`
The Skeletal Jobs screen — for unofficial or emergency assignments.

"Skeletal" jobs are quick assignments that don't go through the normal complaint → job order workflow. They're used when a team is sent out immediately without the formal paperwork.

Key features:
- Create a skeletal job by picking a Leader, Driver (optional), Members, work type, difficulty, damage space, and barangay
- "Mark as Accomplished" button moves it to the Accomplished screen
- Deleted skeletal jobs go to the Trash Bin just like regular job orders


`team_jo.dart`
The Team Status screen — a visual gallery showing each team's job stats.
Shows all teams as cards in a grid. Each card displays the team name, leader avatar, member count, pending vs accomplished counts, and a completion progress bar.

Key features:
- Click any team card to open a -detailed dialog- with tabs for Pending and Accomplished jobs
- The detail dialog shows the full team lineup (leader, driver, members with avatars)
- Includes a difficulty breakdown donut chart per team
- Filter by month or view overall data
- Works independently from the main dashboard filter

`edit_jo_screen.dart`
Admin-only screen for editing teams and personnel. Has two tabs.

Tab 1 — Edit Teams:
- Create new teams with a name, leader, driver, and members
- Edit existing teams — change the lineup, rename the team
- View monthly lineup history — shows a timeline of how the team composition changed month by month
- Every time a team is created or updated, a snapshot is saved to `team_monthly_logs`

Tab 2 — Edit Personnel:
- Add new personnel (Team Leaders, Drivers, Members) with name, contact, address, position, and profile photo
- Edit or delete existing personnel
- Upload/remove profile photos — stored in Supabase Storage bucket `personnel-photos`

This screen is opened from the Admin page under "Edit Teams" and "Edit Personnel".


`admin_page.dart`
The Admin hub — a menu page with tiles linking to all admin sub-sections.
This is what admins see when they click the Admin item in the sidebar. It shows tiles for every admin function. Clicking a tile swaps the content inline (no `Navigator.push`) so the sidebar stays visible the whole time.
Sections:


User Approvals - Review and approve/reject/block new user sign-ups
Team Mobile Accounts - Create/edit/delete field team login accounts for the PAMD Mobile Application.
Edit Teams -Add or edit teams and assign members
Edit Personnel - Add or edit individual field workers
Delete Jobs - Select job orders to move to the Trash Bin
Trash Bin - Restore or permanently delete trashed jobs
Add/Edit Type of Works - Manage the work type dropdown options
Add/Edit Damage Working Space - Manage the damage space dropdown options

The -User Approvals- tile shows a live red badge with the count of pending approvals. This refreshes every time you navigate back to the hub.

 `admin_user_approvals_page.dart`
Where admins review, approve, reject, block, or delete user accounts.**

Has two tabs — -Pending- (accounts waiting for approval) and -All Accounts- (everyone else).

Actions per user:
- Approve — sets `status = 'approved'`, lets the user log in
- Reject - sets `status = 'rejected'`, shows a rejection message on login
- Block — sets `status = 'blocked'`, locks the account
- Roles— opens a dialog to set the user as `user` or `sub_admin` with specific permission checkboxes
- No Photo — removes the user's profile photo URL from the database
- Delete — permanently removes the account row

The -Permissions dialog- for sub-admins lets you toggle:
- Admin Panel Access — can see and use the Admin section
- Edit Reports — can edit monthly, overall, and relocation reports

The pending count syncs automatically with `pendingUsersNotifier` after every action.


`admin_team_accounts_page.dart`
Where admins create and manage login accounts for the field teams' for mobile app.

These accounts are completely separate from the `users` table. They live in the `profiles` table and use **bcrypt-hashed passwords** — no email, no Supabase Auth.

Actions:
- Create Account — picks a team, enters a full name, username, and password (min 6 chars). Password is hashed with bcrypt before saving
- Edit Account — change the username, full name, or team assignment
- Reset Password - enter a new password, re-hashed and saved
- Delete Account — permanently removes the profile row

Accounts without a team assigned show an amber "No team" warning badge.

`admin_work_types_page.dart`
Manages the "Type of Work" dropdown options shown in the Job Order form.

A simple CRUD page — admins can add new work type codes (example: "101"), give them a name, edit existing ones, or delete them. Changes are saved to the `work_types` table and immediately reflected in `workTypesNotifier` so every form dropdown updates without restarting the app.

 `admin_damage_spaces_page.dart`
Manages the "Damaged Working Space" dropdown options in the Job Order form.

Same structure as the work types page but for the `damage_spaces` table. Admins add/edit/delete surface type options (Concrete/Asphalt, Sidewalk/Gutter, Earth, etc.) and they instantly update across the app.

